tools.description:
Accessibility for application windows. Modes: apps lists windows (wN, title, app, active). observe returns the window tree with rN refs. find returns matching rN; a truncated result shows the cursor call for the next page. act runs ordered actions in one window, checks them before input, and reports each target's change, windows opened/closed/focused, and a diff. Copy rN/wN exactly from the latest result; stale refs fail and never rebind. keypress/type without ref go to the focused window. activate/close take a title substring or wN. Put close, and any action that opens or replaces a window, last. until waits for a predicate; false is a result, not an error. Errors return code and hint. Examples:
{"mode":"act","actions":[{"type":"activate","title":"Quarterly report"},{"type":"keypress","keys":["CTRL","S"]}]}
{"mode":"find","window_ref":"w2","query":{"role":"button","name_contains":"Save"}}
{"mode":"act","actions":[{"type":"click","ref":"r12"}],"until":{"type":"title","text":"Export"}}
